            <td data-label="Confidence">{row.conf}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Pay figures here are indicative ranges and averages from public profiles, not exact or guaranteed amounts.
    Pay differs by city, employer, skill and year, and markets change. Check current job listings (for example on
    LinkedIn, Naukri or Indeed) and ask people working in the role before you decide. No India pay figure for
    freelance web design is given because only vendor blogs were found; ask for three written quotes on the same
    scope instead.
  </p>

  <h2 id="web-design">Web design as your first income</h2>

  <p>
    Web design is the quicker route to a paying client, so it works as a bridge into product work. On 17 October
    2026, W3Techs showed WordPress on 39.6% of all websites (58.4% of sites with a known CMS), Shopify 5.3%, Wix
    4.2%, Squarespace 2.4% and Webflow 0.8%, with 32.1% using no CMS it tracks. Plenty of sites exist and plenty
    need fixing.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Getting squeezed</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Plain brochure sites built from a template. Site builders and AI tools do these in an afternoon.</li>
        <li>Competing on the lowest quote on a marketplace.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Still earns</div>
      <ul>
        <li>A clear niche (clinics, schools, local shops, coaches) with a fixed-scope package.</li>
        <li>Page speed, simple copy, booking or payment flow, and a monthly care plan after launch.</li>
        <li>Moving from pages to products: a small tool or dashboard built with the client.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    <strong>Who pays and how they trust you:</strong> the small business owner. They trust a live site they can
    open, a referral, and a person who replies. The first sales skill is a simple offer with a clear price and
    a follow-up message. Rate: <span class="pill pill--blue">Scalable with a business layer</span> (a studio or
    retainers), and <span class="pill pill--gold">Not so scalable</span> as a low-cost solo page builder.
    Once work is regular, check GST and Udyam rules on the official portals.
  </p>

  <h2 id="own-it">Four ways to own the work</h2>

  <p>
    A salary is a tool to save and learn. Ownership comes when you set the price and keep the asset. Each route
    below has a sales layer that most designers are never taught.
  </p>

  <div class="own-grid">
    {ownRows.map((row) => (
      <div class="own-card">
        <span class={`pill pill--${row.label === "Scalable" ? "teal" : "blue"}`}>{row.label}</span>
        <div class="own-card__title">{row.title}</div>
        <p>{row.who}</p>
        <p>{row.trust}</p>
        <p>{row.skill}</p>
        <p>{row.number}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path:</strong> a niche practice that grows into a small studio scales because you set
      the price, package repeat work, hire for the routine parts and earn from retainers instead of single hours.
      It is a choice, not a duty, and no income is promised.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Your growth moves are specific: add a domain (fintech, health, education), learn to read one product metric,
    build a small design system, write clearly in English, and show the work on one platform where your clients
    look. Much of this work can be done remotely when your proof is strong, so check each employer's policy and let your portfolio, not your city, do the talking.
  </p>

