        <li>Designers who can code a working prototype are valued; the reverse is rarer.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Pick a route from the table. Ship one project. Test it on three people who hire designers. If the answers
    are good, spend on feedback or a course. If not, adjust before you pay. Building a skill portfolio with
    proof is how you earn sooner and move toward earlier financial freedom. If you want a second opinion on
    your own situation, try
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>,
    or start with the free
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments/">career and skill assessments</a>.
  </p>

